\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
CCC is regenerated annually in furrows of 7 m
\begin_inset script superscript

\begin_layout Plain Layout
2
\end_layout

\end_inset

 with 20 seed tubers planted per accession.
 Furrows were spaced 1 m apart,
 and plants within the furrows were separated by 0.35 m.
 All accessions were maintained under standard agronomic practices,
 including soil analysis and weekly crop monitoring.
 This regeneration process served as the basis for the morphological color characterization of 599 accessions.
 The evaluations included assessing the uniformity of qualitative plant descriptors and recording the characteristics of randomly selected tubers at the time of harvest.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset ERT
